<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>P divides AB internally in the ratio <m>{2} : {3}</m>, and <m>\overrightarrow{OA} = \mathbf{a}</m> and <m>\overrightarrow{OB} = \mathbf{b}</m>. Complete the working.</p><div>(a) <m>\overrightarrow{AP} =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/> <m>\overrightarrow{AB}</m> (a fraction)  </div><div>(b) <m>\overrightarrow{AB} =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="ans2"/>  </div><div>(c) <m>\overrightarrow{OP} = \overrightarrow{OA} + \overrightarrow{AP} = \mathbf{a} + \dfrac{ {2} }{ {5} }(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}) =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The ratio <m>{2} : {3}</m> splits AB into <m>{5}</m> equal parts and AP is <m>{2}</m> of them, so <m>\overrightarrow{AP} = \dfrac{ {2} }{ {5} }\,\overrightarrow{AB}</m>.</p><p>(b) End minus start: <m>\overrightarrow{AB} = \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}</m>.</p><p>(c) <m>\mathbf{a} + \dfrac{ {2} }{ {5} }(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}) = \left(1 - \dfrac{ {2} }{ {5} }\right)\mathbf{a} + \dfrac{ {2} }{ {5} }\mathbf{b} = {\frac{2 \mathbf{b}}{5}+\frac{3 \mathbf{a}}{5}}</m>. This is the ratio theorem: <m>\overrightarrow{OP} = \dfrac{n\mathbf{a} + m\mathbf{b}}{m + n}</m>. The weight on <m>\mathbf{a}</m> is the part of the ratio nearer B.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{2}{5}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\mathbf{b}-\mathbf{a}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{2 \mathbf{b}}{5}+\frac{3 \mathbf{a}}{5}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>